# jfeelgood.com

Static site for JFeelgood — paintings, the Self Work series, books, and limited-edition collectible art cards. Served from this repository (GitHub Pages user site, custom domain jfeelgood.com).

## Pages

- `index.html` — the title screen and the explorable 3D planet (Three.js/WebGL2). Every visitor lands on a title screen offering **ENTER THE WORLD** or **CLASSIC SITE**; nothing heavy loads until the world is chosen. Bootstraps `planet/js/main.js`; the on-terrain content zones (billboards, gallery rotunda, Self Work, books, collect, NOVA), a vehicle **garage** (drone/plane/tank/motorcycle — walk up and press E to pilot, third-person chase cam), and streaming biome foliage (forest/desert/plains/alpine) all live under `planet/js/`. Only browsers without WebGL2 are sent to the classic-only card.
- **Mobile.** Phones and tablets run the same world. A head probe in `index.html` sets `html.touch` on touch-primary devices (`pointer: coarse` **and** `hover: none`, so touchscreen laptops keep the desktop path). `planet/js/touch.js` then draws an on-screen thumbstick, drag-to-look, and ▲/RUN/ACT buttons that write into the same `input` singleton the keyboard fills — so `walk.js`, `gallery.js` and `vehicles.js` are untouched. Touch also boots the `low` quality tier (pixel ratio 1, no shadows, no bloom) with reduced dressing and foliage budgets. `hud.js` swaps the keyboard glyphs in prompts, hints and card copy for their on-screen equivalents.
- **Val Feelgood ski resort.** `planet/js/skislope.js` self-sites a snow mountain on the cold plains (same site-scan pattern as Mont Le Ringger, biased toward the ice caps): one pure height function is the mesh, the collision floor and the scatter — including the groomed piste, three kickers and a half-pipe carved into it. A rideable chairlift (ambient looping chairs; E at the base station to board, auto-unload at the summit) leads to the Summit Shack, where a dialogue rents a **snowboard** — a vehicle whose def carries its own physics (gravity along the slope gradient, carving, momentum-driven air off the lips), with C toggling first/third-person. The resort registers a snow-biased weather region and exposes `window.__skiSlope` (teleports, `drop()`, `probe()`); `?debug=at:ski` jumps to the base lodge.
- **Query params** (all on `index.html`): `?debug` skips the title screen and enters the world headlessly, exposing `window.__debug` (`walk`, `input`, `quality()`, `sim(seconds)`, `interact()`); `?debug=at:<zone>` jumps to a zone (`at:ski` for the resort); `?fly` is a noclip camera; `?touch` / `?notouch` force the mobile path on or off for testing.
- `classic.html` — single-page gallery: hero (Dreamfall), featured works carousel, story of growth carousel, Collect section (limited-edition cards), archives promo, Self Work carousel, books, about, NOVA 7.
- `archives.html` — "Archives Wall": masonry grid of 186 paintings (2004–2025), rendered from lazy-loaded WebP thumbnails that click through to full-resolution originals.
- `llms.txt` — machine-readable summary for AI crawlers. Keep it in sync with the real pages and products.
- `robots.txt` / `sitemap.xml` — standard crawl config.

## Assets

- `assets/images/` — full-resolution originals (kept as the archive of record; referenced by pages only as click-through targets).
- `assets/images/opt/` — 1200px-wide WebP derivatives used by index.html, plus `og-jfeelgood.jpg` (social share image).
- `assets/images/archives/thumbs/` — 700px-wide WebP thumbnails used by the archives grid.
- `assets/images/cards/` — 640px WebP product shots for the Collect section (sourced from the minicuration repo).

Derivatives are generated with Pillow (resize + WebP). If you add a new painting image, add an optimized copy in the matching derivative folder and reference that from the HTML.

## Commerce

The Collect section sells limited-edition art cards (editions of 50, $23) fulfilled by the sister site minicuration.com:

- Buy buttons are Stripe Payment Links (one per design) with `?client_reference_id=jfeelgood` for sales attribution in Stripe.
- Live availability ("X of 50 claimed") is fetched from `https://minicuration.com/api/stock`; that endpoint allowlists this site's origins for CORS. If the fetch fails, static "Limited edition of 50" text remains.
- Product data (names, slugs, payment links) must match the minicuration repo (`api/webhook.js` is the canonical map there).

## Styling

`classic.html` and `archives.html` keep their CSS inline in each page's `<style>` block; the world's CSS lives in `planet/css/planet.css` (title screen, HUD, cards, the `#touch` control layer, and the `html.touch` / `@media` mobile rules). Fonts: Cormorant Garamond + DM Sans via Google Fonts (linked in `<head>`). Dark palette on index.html (`--accent: #f5b642`), light paper palette on archives.html.
